os  where i'm just like talking and  delivering value i try to outsource most  of that i've gotten to a point where i  can outsource almost 100 of those videos  i rarely need to touch those videos i  just film it send the footage i've  already created the templates and the  structure and editing guidelines like i  don't really need to spend time working  on those for the more high quality  videos like the architecture videos that  i release on a monthly or bi-monthly  basis those ones actually i have a more  experienced editor that i've been  working with here in vancouver and we  are actually in the process of starting  a film company called noli media i will  leave the links  to the website in the description if you  want to check it out but the goal is for  us to create yeah these more high  production quality documentary style  architectural videos and yeah we're both  really interested in exploring the  filmmaking side of architecture and how  we can tell a visual story of  architecture typically what happens is  i'll create the script and for those  videos it's like very very tightly  scripted  so i'll spend most of my time on the  script and the research and i'll  storyboard the videos and kind of plan  out like what i would like to see in  each area what type of b-rolls what kind  of imagery what kind of music and then i  start to work with my editor on the  editing process and i pass off the  footage and the script to him and he  starts the editing process and it's kind  of a back and forth from there and so  that is a more intensive editing process  and the way i've structured my channel  is that i'll have a couple of videos  where i'm just like delivering value  it's mostly me talking in front of the  camera and then i'll have something  around like one out of four videos that  are these like more high production  quality videos which are the videos that  i'm personally like more interested in  making this balance helps me have a more  sustainable  channel and a more sustainable you know  work-life balance and yeah i think  that's how i'm able to make it work hi  danny here's my question if you could go  back 10 years and give yourself one  piece of advice it could be architecture  related or youtube related what would it  be hey anthony by the way guys anthony  went to architecture school with me  years and years and years ago  and he also has an awesome youtube  channel uh you guys should check it out  so that is a tough question if i could  give myself one piece of advice and one  only this will be  by bitcoin  joking this question actually made me do  some serious reflection because it's  really asking you know if there's one  thing and one piece of information i  could have known ten years ago that  would have had the most positive impact  on my life  what would it be so ten years ago  that's around the time i would have  started architecture school and i think  one of the biggest and best realizations  of my life  is that ultimately people only care  about their own problems and their own  [ __ ] that's going on in their lives and  mostly they're gonna forget about all  the dumb [ __ ] you've done unless you  slap the mc at the oscars i feel like i  wasted a lot of time looking for the  approval of other people but in the end  i just needed approval from myself  and  one of the best  things i did was  kind of  shut down that part of my brain that was  constantly worried about what other  people thought and start this youtube  channel it has really  rewarded me handsomely  so  that's the advice that i would give  myself  10 years ago so i have two announcements  before we continue i was super excited  to get your questions but what do you  notice only one girl  sent me a video and i know for a fact  that i have a 60 40 male-to-female ratio  on my channel from my youtube analytics  and i've gotten so many questions from  female subscribers this is actually a  very common scenario like women are  often very under